{
 "note": "One pack's ledger, carved from the 13:14 read in captures/bms-frames.jsonl and re-laid onto a regular hourly timeline. Every record is 24 bytes the pack itself wrote; only the RTC counter at bytes[0..3] is rewritten, so each row still decodes to the voltages, currents, capacities, cell extremes and temperatures of the reading it came from. A 0x06 record carries no ASCII and no serial, which is the basis detailLogFrame.json is committed verbatim on and is re-verified byte-wise over exactly these rows. scripts/visual-check.mjs seeds them into the ring stores, sliding the whole ledger — counters and read stamp together — onto the day the check runs.",
 "scenario": "Six days, five of them recorded: one day, then a day the pack recorded nothing, then three days to now. A cell-4 overcharge trip fires at the top of a charge, the hour before it snaps the coulomb counter to exactly nominal, and one clock rewrite of 7 h 01 m 08 s splits the ledger into two faces. The read that filed it measured the pack running between 6 h 16 m and 7 h 16 m ahead of the browser, which is the interval the captured read really gave. The unrecorded day is the one part of this that is arranged rather than observed: the captured ring holds no hole but the rewrite itself, so this file is not evidence about the pack's sampling and must not be cited as any.",
 "deviceKey": "jk:DEMO00000000001",
